      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do ?\n\nMake `TestFlextronRouter::test_gumbel_determinism` deterministic by controlling the Python `random` draw that selects the router hard/soft branch.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: Fixes #5155\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [ ] I have added relevant unit tests\n  - N/A: this is a test-only fix that updates an existing unit test and removes the `flaky_in_dev` quarantine once the test controls the extra Python RNG source.\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n  - N/A: this PR only fixes a unit-test flake and does not change production training behavior or numerics.\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code [Typing guidelines](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html)\n  - N/A: no public API, production code, or type signatures changed.\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n  - N/A: no user-facing behavior or docs surface changed.\n- [x] I have run the [autoformatter.sh](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/tools/autoformat.sh) on my PR\n\n## Summary\n\n`test_gumbel_determinism` compares two `FlextronRouter` instances bit-for-bit after copying weights. The Gumbel path is torch-seeded, but `FlextronRouter.forward()` also samples `hard_sample` from Python `random.random()`. If the two forwards draw different hard/soft branches, the bit-exact assertion can fail even though the Gumbel seed path is deterministic.\n\nThis change seeds Python `random` identically before each router forward in the test, restores the previous Python RNG state afterward, and removes the `flaky_in_dev` quarantine. Production router behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `uv run isort --check-only tests/unit_tests/elastification/test_hybrid_flex_router.py`\n- [x] `uv run python -m py_compile tests/unit_tests/elastification/test_hybrid_flex_router.py`\n- [x] `git diff --check`\n- [x] `PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh`\n  - `black`, `isort`, `pylint`, and `ruff` passed for the changed file.\n  - The script reached `mypy`, but local `.venv` does not contain `mypy`; the repository script handles this with `|| true` and exits 0.\n- [x] `uv run python - <<'PY' ...` verified `random.seed(0)` produces the same `hard_sample` draw (`0.84442185152504812`, below `hard_sample_th=0.996`) for both forwards.\n- [ ] `uv run python -m pytest -q tests/unit_tests/elastification/test_hybrid_flex_router.py::TestFlextronRouter::test_gumbel_determinism` did not run locally: the local uv environment fails while loading `tests/unit_tests/conftest.py` with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'torch'`. This machine also has no local NVIDIA GPU, so the CUDA-backed target test needs CI validation.\n",
